# The code that reaches a collider or a collider's box (`.collider(`, `.colliders()`, `.by_id(`,
# `get::<Collider>`, `.aabb_min`, `.aabb_max`, the `PhysicsWorld::` paths of the first three, and a
# `&Collider` in a query or an argument) in `crates/*/src` outside `shards_motion/src/physics/`. A
# voxel field is no collider, has no box and is no entity with a `Collider`: such a line is right
# only where a field cannot be what it looks at, or where it leaves fields out on purpose.
# `tests/readers.rs` fails on a line that is not here and on a row here that matches no line, so a
# new reader comes with its reason (the voxel design, 6.3).
#
# One row per line: file :: the line's text, trimmed :: why a field does not need it. A line the
# file has twice is listed twice. Code that reads the solid under a hit asks
# `PhysicsWorld::extent_at`, `top_under` or `solid_span`.

